  introduction: Harihara is a composite form that combines the Hindu deities Shiva and Vishnu into a single representation. This sandstone relief presents the divine figure surrounded by an elaborate arrangement of smaller carved figures and decorative details.
  culturalSignificance: Harihara represents the complementary aspects of Shiva and Vishnu. The combined form is an expression of the relationship between Shaivism and Vaishnavism in Hindu religious traditions.
